 =========================================
 C O N C E P T U A L   D F T   ( F D L ) 
 =========================================
 Originally written by Laurens Groot (SCM) for condensed Fukui functions
 Extended to other descriptors by L. Joubert & V. Tognetti - Univ.Rouen, France
 All results in a.u. (except dissociation energies in eV)
 All calculations are based on a finite difference linearization (FDL) approach
 Condensed (atomic) values are obtained using four different partitions of the
 electronic density: Hirshfeld, Mulliken, Voronoï and QTAIM

 General reviews on CDFT:
 ------------------------
 H. Chermette, J. Comput. Chem. 20, 129 (1999)
 P. Geerlings, F. de Proft, W. Langenaecker, Chem. Rev. 103, 1793 (2003)

 All formulas used for ADF calculations can be found in this reference:
 G. Hoffmann, V. Tognetti and L. Joubert, J. Mol. Model. 24, 281 (2018)


